L(378, "- **Admission and capture terms** [proposed, NP1.10(ac)]", r'''
- **Admission and capture terms** [proposed, NP1.10(ac)]: the admission bounds (D118 and N1.5), overage disabled, the freshness age (D136) and margin, the keep-awake policy, the capture rules, the context mode and the quiet account (amendment N1's item (ad)) apply unchanged to every pilot and production attempt. D111, D118 and D136 were decided for the canary, and amendment N1's items are ratified for the canary (D138); applying them here is this amendment's proposal. The dollar guard and the deadline are NP1.10(ab)'s subject, not this item's. N1.5 argues the admission bounds for a run of up to 21,600 s. They are thresholds at the start of a run, with no term for its length, so they can be applied to a 43,200 s run as written; whether they are the right values for it is not derived again here. **One native attempt at a time follows from the quiet account:** a second attempt would be a session drawing on the registered account.
''')
